# doc-sensitive-paths — sensitive-path list for the vendored doc-check.sh
# (shipping-work-python-fastapi Step 1.5). One path per line; blank lines and
# `#`-comments ignored. This file REPLACES the script's built-in defaults
# rather than extending them (gregoryfoster/skills#252, #172).
#
# Entries match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth, not just the start of the
# path. Do not re-anchor them; over-matching a spot-check that asks a human to
# look is the cheap failure, under-matching is the expensive one.
#
# Inclusion rule: a path belongs here when its *inventory* — the names,
# existence, or structure of its files — is mirrored in a doc that would go
# stale if it changed. tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py asserts that every
# entry present here matches at least one tracked file at test time, which is
# what stops individual entries going inert the way 6 of the 12 upstream
# defaults had in this tree. It does not police what the list omits.
#
# When this check fires, spot-check the doc sections that own the changed path:
#
#   AGENTS.md            architecture diagram, frozen/derived table,
#                        conventions, infra + env tables, common tasks, skills
#   README.md            Project Structure tree, test-file table, CLI list,
#                        features, API endpoint tables
#   docs/SCHEMA.md       table/column reference + migration history
#                        (alembic/versions/)
#   docs/DEPLOYMENT.md   systemd services and ops reference (infra/)
#   docs/SKILLS.md       skill descriptions and trigger phrases (skills/)
#   docs/STYLE.md        brand colors and CSS conventions (static/, templates/)

# --- Root inventory + config files --------------------------------------------
AGENTS.md
README.md
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
package.json
.env.example
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- Trees whose file inventory is documented ---------------------------------
src/wslcb_licensing_tracker/
templates/
static/
tests/
# NB: segment-matched, so scripts/ also catches the skill wrappers under
# skills/*/scripts/, which README does not inventory. Comments must be
# whole-line — doc-check.sh does not strip trailing ones, so an inline comment
# becomes part of the entry and silently matches nothing.
scripts/
infra/
alembic/versions/

# --- Agent-context surface (AGENTS.md + docs/SKILLS.md name these by file) ----
skills/
.claude/hooks/

